{"title":"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems/N1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that there is no positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a44f5a828ac0a2029309817cf345d017ddf28232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1,2,\\ldots,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />, the leftmost digit (in decimal notation) of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273b131e30a4284da978609b6345d2eca3f63293.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + k)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that there is such a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08818f2458fdeb549571711cc73d631ea254475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 8)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f95fd528b3d9bdfb1c3c46eea0847b75017cd41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Then we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b630d5f16b946f864d7d3f0b4e448d66593c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot 10^{a-1} \\leqslant (n + 8)! &lt; 9 \\cdot 10^{a-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"21\" /> \n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d8cb8be9d263128e989aa1df5e56ea001ffdd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{b-1} \\leqslant n + 9 &lt; 10^b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Combining these inequalities via multiplication we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9154d2130cdc2603f71583ba8848008e2a9b1e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot 10^{a+b-2} \\leqslant (n+9)! &lt; 9 \\cdot 10^{a+b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"274\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>From this inequality, it can be seen that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a991aa96da2e2197e735fc85d6d6678e6fdb505c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+9)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> has at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/2433b45f309883be223f2a0f0391d7f22eb9ab6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> and at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> digits. However, if it has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> digits then the first digit is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which contradicts with how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is defined. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a991aa96da2e2197e735fc85d6d6678e6fdb505c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+9)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/2433b45f309883be223f2a0f0391d7f22eb9ab6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> digits. Expressing this as an inequality, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef96f21bc04d64689840707fe19519384c784823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 10^{a+b-2} \\leqslant (n+9)! &lt; 10^{a+b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Combining these values with the earlier bounds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f2d99c90cbaf9d2fbfc51be849fec4ccb5b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+8)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> via division, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e23c7638349e6b05b52b1bbfa56448d61302017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{b-1} &lt; n+9 &lt; \\frac{5}4 10^{b - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1f0ce933d1741ce6ef4289924d963386fc458e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1 &lt; 10^{b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"19\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce34bf63ea632e9813707fd41b49c0c5ae31584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b5f8d61bb40eb3fa458bb0c5e75ae5aaed605b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, one of the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d745f5baa33f9757175ac6ad8bf48d526ba1ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2,n+2,\\ldots n+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"17\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce34bf63ea632e9813707fd41b49c0c5ae31584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{b-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" />. Call that value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82297192d00cd2fd4a348c5417f8dd2d50fef92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+l &amp;nbsp; (1 &lt; l &lt; 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />. This means that the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522b869e61970fa3854c9e4577985178fc267b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+l)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> are just the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd5ce17eb071b02aa23b3339ab876a75b7b5a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+l-1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />, followed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3dcf0896441c33c0dcf7e4616e114e9326bb6b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> zeroes. Thus the first digit of the two numbers are equal, which contradicts with how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is defined.\nThis means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/059a21370b0e1740df16da87eb95b90db75f7795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{b-1} \\leqslant n+1 &lt; n+2 &lt; n+3 &lt; n+4 &lt; n+9 &lt; \\frac{5}4 10^{b - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"455\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89b67130cb00a3a5016e838246d054737368fb37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />. Then we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cba27d9c05b0f7da443f204ad53203aed38092db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{c-1} \\leqslant (n+1)! &lt; 2 \\cdot 10^{c-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"218\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Combining these with the bounds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70670f99b13b346e700d7fec74ab5b49061d4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46aba6908f07148ec36b64bdeb19704eba9fef40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> via multiplication we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/010b6465366a5624e26d984b3d5df9479278e173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{c+3b-4} \\leqslant (n+4)! &lt; \\frac{125}{32}10^{c+3b-4} &lt; 4 \\cdot 10^{c+3b-4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"383\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b8cbe77691403c22746af5d0b2845359bbf9a6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 4)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a53b99d9fa03c10936593c8b525f1fa028326b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+3b-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> digits, but is smaller than the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a53b99d9fa03c10936593c8b525f1fa028326b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+3b-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> digit number with the first digit 4, which means that its first digit can't be 4. This contradicts with how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is defined, thus no such value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> exists.\n</p><p>~Circling\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/N1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2001 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=17470\">Discussion on AOPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017060937\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 243/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8685/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7197:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017060937 and revision id 284347. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}